---
title: Scenes
sidebar:
  order: 9
---

A scene is an EVT script that takes control from the player to tell part of the story: NPCs move and talk, and the camera moves to show them. This example plays the first time the player enters a map. An NPC walks up to the player while the camera follows, says a message, and the scene saves a game flag so it never plays again.

The example uses Goompa's sprite and a message from the base game. `NPC_Goompa` is an NPC you add to the map, as [NPCs](/papermario-dx/world/npcs/) describes, and `GF_KMR99_MetGoompa` is a game flag you add, as [Saved flags and bytes](/papermario-dx/save-data/game-flags/) describes.

## Writing a scene

```c
EvtScript EVS_Scene_MeetGoompa = {
    Call(DisablePlayerInput, true)
    Wait(10)
    // the camera moves to where Goompa will stop, while he walks there
    Thread
        Call(UseSettingsFrom, CAM_DEFAULT, 60, 0, 0)
        Call(SetPanTarget, CAM_DEFAULT, 60, 0, 0)
        Call(SetCamDistance, CAM_DEFAULT, Float(300.0))
        Call(SetCamSpeed, CAM_DEFAULT, Float(2.0))
        Call(PanToTarget, CAM_DEFAULT, 0, true)
    EndThread
    Call(SetNpcAnimation, NPC_Goompa, ANIM_Goompa_Walk)
    Call(SetNpcSpeed, NPC_Goompa, Float(2.0))
    Call(NpcMoveTo, NPC_Goompa, 60, 0, 0)
    Call(SetNpcAnimation, NPC_Goompa, ANIM_Goompa_Idle)
    Call(WaitForCam, CAM_DEFAULT, Float(1.0))
    // talk
    Call(PlayerFaceNpc, NPC_Goompa, 0)
    Call(SpeakToPlayer, NPC_Goompa, ANIM_Goompa_Talk, ANIM_Goompa_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_001C)
    // give the camera back
    Call(ResetCam, CAM_DEFAULT, Float(4.0))
    Set(GF_KMR99_MetGoompa, true)
    Call(DisablePlayerInput, false)
    Return
    End
};
```

Step by step, the scene:

1. Stops the player from moving with `DisablePlayerInput`, so they can't walk away or open menus during the scene.
2. Starts the camera panning in a `Thread`, so it moves while Goompa walks. To do more things at once, see [Threads](/papermario-dx/evt-scripts/threads/).
3. Walks Goompa to a point with `NpcMoveTo`, which takes an X and Z position, and how many frames the walk takes. With `0` frames, Goompa walks at the speed from `SetNpcSpeed`. Moving an NPC doesn't change its animation, so the scene sets his walking animation before the walk and his idle animation after it.
4. Waits until the camera arrives with `WaitForCam`.
5. Turns the player to face Goompa, and has Goompa speak with `SpeakToPlayer`, which waits until the player closes the message. For more ways to show messages, see [Speech](/papermario-dx/messages/speech/).
6. Pans the camera back to the player and gives it back to the map's zones with `ResetCam`. For more about moving the camera, see [Camera](/papermario-dx/world/camera/).
7. Sets the game flag, then gives control back to the player.

## Playing the scene when the player enters the map

Start the scene after the player walks in, if the flag isn't set:

```c
EvtScript EVS_EnterMap = {
    Set(LVar0, Ref(EVS_BindExitTriggers))
    ExecWait(EnterWalk)
    IfEq(GF_KMR99_MetGoompa, false)
        Exec(EVS_Scene_MeetGoompa)
    EndIf
    Return
    End
};
```

In `EVS_Main`, replace the `Set(LVar0, Ref(EVS_BindExitTriggers))` and `Exec(EnterWalk)` lines with `Exec(EVS_EnterMap)`. `ExecWait` waits until the player has walked in, so the scene doesn't start while they're still walking. For more about entering a map, see [Entries and exits](/papermario-dx/world/entries-and-exits/).

If the scene is part of the main story, check and set `GB_StoryProgress` instead of a flag of its own, as [Saved flags and bytes](/papermario-dx/save-data/game-flags/#story-progress) describes.

## Testing the scene

With the map's `main.c` open, select **Game > Play**. The scene plays unless the save you play from already has the flag set, such as when you saved after the scene played.
